  "summary": "Four of the five top-ranked documents directly apply graph neural network message passing over relational graphs to predicting protein molecular function, which is the closest available match to the research question about GNNs applied to protein function. [V0145] (Gupta et al., 2024) achieves the highest reported accuracy of 0.92 on the ProtMap dataset. [V0148] (Brennan et al., 2018) reports F1=0.78 on MetroFlow. [V0147] (Adebayo et al., 2026) reports AUROC=0.71 on ChurnBench. [V0146] (Haddad et al., 2025) reports MAE=0.64 on FireScope. The fifth document [V0158] (Chen et al., 2019) also addresses predicting protein molecular function but uses boosted decision-tree ensembles rather than GNNs, making it the weakest match; it is included because it still targets the protein function topic and rounds out the five candidates. No other candidates in the supplied set address protein function with graph-based methods.",
